{
  "id": "DP11Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Skin lesion removal",
  "description": "Skin lesion removal is an outpatient procedure to surgically remove benign or malignant skin lesions. Your dermatologist removes the lesion under local anesthesia, taking care to remove it completely with appropriate margins. The wound is closed with stitches or left to heal naturally depending on the lesion's size and location. Healing typically takes one to three weeks. The cost of this procedure may vary depending on the size of the area being treated. Categories include small (<2cm), medium (2-4cm), and large (>4cm).",
